        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Object And Object Id Identifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774266145160"
          },
          "code": "OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER",
          "id": "1763119304324",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763119304327_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intelligent agent that identifies object and objectId from given input. \nTake this user query as input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nUse following instructions or examples to identify object and objectId\n*   Analyze the user's query to identify the HCM object type and its corresponding ID.\n    *   **Apply the following mapping rules to determine the 'object' and 'objectId' for the 'ConflictDetection' tool:**\n        *   If the conversation is about an **assignment**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_ALL_ASSIGNMENTS_M\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'assignmentId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about a **person**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PERSONS\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'personId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about a **goal**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"HRG_GOAL_PLN_ASSIGNMENTS\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'goalId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **phones**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PHONES\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'phoneId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **address**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_ADDRESSES_F\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'address_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **person names**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PERSON_NAMES_F\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'person_name_id' extracted from the user's input\n        *   If the conversation is about **national identifiers**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_NATIONAL_IDENTIFIERS\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'national_identifier_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **visas**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_VISAS_PERMITS_F\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'visa_permit_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **legislatives**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PEOPLE_LEGISLATIVE_F\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'person_legislative_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **emails**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"PER_EMAIL_ADDRESSES\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'email_address_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **documents**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"HR_DOCUMENTS_OF_RECORD\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'documents_of_record_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **salary**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"CMP_SALARY\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'salary_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **compensation**:\n            *   Set 'object' to \"CMP_VC_PER_ELIG_PLANS\"\n            *   Set 'objectId' to the 'assignment_id' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **location**:\n             *   Set 'object' to \"PER_LOCATIONS\"\n             *   Set 'objectId' to the 'locationid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **contract**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PERIODS_OF_SERVICE\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'contractid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **job**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_JOBS_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'jobid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **position**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"HR_ALL_POSITIONS_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'positionid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **grade ladder**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_GRADE_LADDERS_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'grade ladderid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **grade**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_GRADES_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'gradeid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **oraganization**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"HR_ALL_ORGANIZATION_UNITS_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'oraganizationid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **grade rate**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_RATES_F_VL\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'grade rateid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Citizenship**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_CITIZENSHIPS\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'citizenshipid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Passport**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PASSPORTS\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'passportid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Driver licence**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_DRIVERS_LICENSES\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'licenseid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Demographic**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PEOPLE_LEGISLATIVE_F\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'Demographicid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Disability Info**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_DISABILITIES_F\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'Disabilityid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Change Photo**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_IMAGES\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'photoid' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Share Data Info**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_SHARE_INFORMATION\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'ShareInfoId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Person External Identifier**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_EXT_APP_IDENTIFIERS\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'external identifierId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **BiographicInfo**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_ALL_PEOPLE_F\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'BiographicId' extracted from the user's input.\n        *   If the conversation is about **Additional person Info\"**:\n              *   Set 'object' to \"PER_PEOPLE_EXTRA_INFO_F\"\n              *   Set 'objectId' to the 'Additional Person InfoId' extracted from the user's input.\n\n\n**Example Interaction Flow:**\n\n*   **User Input:** \"Check for conflicts.\"\n*   **Agent Output:** \"I need both the object type (e.g., 'person', 'assignment', 'goal', 'phone') and its corresponding ID to check for pending transactions. Could you please provide them?\"\n\n*   **User Input:** \"Check if a person has any pending transactions.\" (Missing ID)\n*   **Agent Output:** \"I need both the object type (e.g., 'person', 'assignment', 'goal', 'phone') and its corresponding ID to check for pending transactions. Could you please provide them?\"\n\n*   **User Input:** \"Check if person with ID 12345 has any pending transactions.\"\n*   **Agent Output:** (object=\"PER_PERSONS\", objectId=\"12345\")"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"LLMObjectIdResponse\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"object\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"objectId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"object\", \"objectId\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is Object Id There"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1763375471498",
            "false": "1774266283079"
          },
          "code": "IS_OBJECT_ID_THERE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1765183892456",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765183892459_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.VALIDATEOBJECTID.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_HCM_GLOBALHUMA_CONFLICTSDETECT",
            "functionName": "get_conflicts_for_object_objectId",
            "name": "Conflict Detection"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763380657997"
          },
          "code": "CONFLICT_DETECTION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765183953521",
          "id": "1763375471498",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763375500604_1",
              "name": "object",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.object}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1763375500604_2",
              "name": "objectId",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.objectId}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format Output"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_OUTPUT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765183953521",
          "id": "1763380657997",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763380657998_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Take this response as input {{$context.$nodes.CONFLICT_DETECTION.$output}}\n\nYou have to summarize the input. \nLook inside input and do the following \n1. If pendingTxnsPresent is false then return \"No matching transactions are found for object = {{$context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.object}} and objectId = {{$context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.objectId}}\"\n\n2. IfpendingTxnsPresent is true then there will be a transactionId as well in the input, fetch this transaction id and add it while returning the output. \nIn this case return - \"Matching transaction with transaction id = transactionId is found for the object with the objectId = {{$context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.objectId}}\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ValidateObjectId",
            "returnType": "boolean",
            "sourceCode": "const objId = $context.$nodes.OBJECT_AND_OBJECT_ID_IDENTIFIER.$output.objectId\n\n// Basic presence check\nif (objId === null || objId === undefined || objId === \"\" ) {\n   return false;\n}\n\nconst str = String(objId).trim();\nif (str.length === 0) {\n  return false;\n}\n\n\n// Numeric check (rejects NaN, Infinity, non-numeric strings)\nconst num = Number(objId);\nif (!Number.isFinite(num)) {\n  return false;\n}\n\n// Optional: if you require an integer (common for IDs), enforce it\nif (!Number.isInteger(num)) {\n  return false;\n}\n\n// Optional: if you require positive IDs\nif (num <= 0) {\n return false;\n}\n\nreturn true;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765183892456"
          },
          "code": "VALIDATEOBJECTID",
          "id": "1774266145160",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Object Not Found Format"
          },
          "outcomes": {
